v0.11.4: close the manager-effect loop — harness, viz, xaman_ek digest

v0.11.3 shipped the substrate for the football-manager metric — a
schema column, an admin inbox, dynamic roster injection. v0.11.4
closes the loop so the metric flows end-to-end, and gives xaman_ek
the same live-context treatment fermi got at a fraction of the tokens.

Item 1 — Fermi console populates counterfactual_probability
- crates/fermi-console/src/api/client.rs: new
  CreateForecastRequest.counterfactual_probability: Option<f64>,
  serde-skipped when None so pre-v0.11.4 servers still accept.
- CockpitState::naive_counterfactual_probability(&self) returns
  question.base_rate.historical_frequency clamped to [0,1] via the
  existing clamp_wire_probability. This is the classic Tetlock/
  Kahneman outside-view baseline — what a naive model would have
  predicted without Fermi's decomposition and specialists.
- Wired into persist_backend_save (draft POST) and publish_forecast
  (publish POST). POST-only: the counterfactual is defined at
  forecast-creation-time and is not touched on PUT. Later
  "Update outside rate" mutations don't retroactively change the
  naive baseline for a row that already exists.
- Honest gap: drafts saved before orchestrate get NULL cf_prob
  because the base rate isn't set yet. We do NOT backfill on later
  PUTs; whatever base rate is in RAM at PUT time isn't the
  counterfactual "at creation time" the metric measures.
- Rationale for base-rate baseline over "naive average of specialist
  outputs": specialists produce driver multipliers on the base rate,
  not stand-alone probabilities. There's no naive arithmetic mean
  of multipliers that maps to a probability without reconstructing
  the FPL model — which is what the counterfactual should strip out.

Item 2 — Manager Effect on /agent/fermi
- New endpoint GET /api/orchestras/:name/manager-effect?limit=N.
  Anonymous-visible. Requires the orchestra to have a strategist
  (400 with message otherwise). Aggregates over resolved forecasts
  matched by agents_used @> [{"agent_name": strategist}] — GIN-
  index-backed via mig-168, so O(rows-matching) not O(table).
  Returns n_resolved, n_with_counterfactual, mean_brier,
  mean_counterfactual, mean_manager_effect, and forecasts[] with
  per-row brier / cf_brier / manager_effect delta.
- New Manager Effect section on templates/agent_detail.html
  Overview tab. Rendered ONLY for agents in STRATEGIST_ORCHESTRAS
  (currently {fermi: "fermi"}) — non-strategists never see it.
- UI: five stat cards (Resolved, With counterfactual, Mean Brier,
  Mean counterfactual, Mean manager effect). Delta card coloured
  green when negative (beat baseline), red when positive.
- Delta bar chart (inline SVG ~640×120): one bar per paired
  forecast, chronological oldest → newest. Bars extend downward
  from mid-line for negative deltas (green wins), upward for
  positive (red losses). Hover tooltips carry question + numbers.
- Recent-resolutions table (last 10) with question link and
  colour-coded delta.
- Empty-state box when no forecasts carry counterfactuals yet.

Item 3 — Xaman Ek digest injection
- inject_orchestra_context refactored to dispatch on strategy per
  strategist:
    enum InjectionStrategy {
        FullRoster { view },
        TierDigest { view, exemplars_per_tier },
    }
- Fermi: FullRoster on orchestra_fermi_members (unchanged).
- Xaman Ek: TierDigest on orchestra_xaman_ek_members with 8
  exemplars per tier.
- Digest format: header line with grand total, one line per tier
  with count and alphabetical sample, closing nudge to use
  `list_agents` for anything beyond the digest.
- One SQL round-trip: array_agg FILTER over a row_number-partitioned
  subselect gives first-N-per-tier without Rust-side sorting.
- Deterministic tier order (system → curated → community) helps
  LLM prompt caching.
- Bounded output regardless of catalogue size (~500 tokens at
  500+ members). Same never-fails guardrails as FullRoster.

Migrations: none. Item 1 is client-only. Item 2 uses v0.11.3 + mig-172
columns and mig-168 GIN index. Item 3 uses the existing xaman_ek view.

